content.text:
45 commands (id — label [menu] (shortcut) params; * = undoable):
node.set* — Set properties name, visible, locked, opacity (0-1 or "50%"), blend, x, y (relative to the parent frame; groups don't count), width, height, rotation (degrees), fills (paints or colours; gradients as {type: linearGradient|radialGradient|angularGradient|diamondGradient, stops: ["#hex", ...], from?, to?} too), fill (colour, {$var: variable id or name}, or "none"/null: no fill), strokes, stroke (colour, {$var: variable id or name}, or "none"/null: no stroke), strokeWeight, strokeAlign (inside|center|outside), strokeSides [t,r,b,l], strokeTopWeight / strokeRightWeight / strokeBottomWeight / strokeLeftWeight (one side; turns on individual strokes), strokeCap / startCap / endCap, strokeJoin, miterAngle (degrees: sharper joins bevel; or miterLimit as a ratio), dashes [..], dashCap (none|round|square; null: dashes take startCap and endCap), widthProfile (preset uniform|wedge|taper|eye|rounded|pinch, [[t, scale], ...] or null), brush (preset id, {preset, spacing, sizeJitter, rotationJitter, scatter, seed} or null), cornerRadius (n or [tl,tr,br,bl]), cornerSmoothing (0-1), effects, clip, isMask, layout (null|horizontal|vertical|grid|{...}), gap, crossGap, padding (n or [t,r,b,l]), paddingTop/Right/Bottom/Left, mainAlign (min|center|max, or the auto gaps spaceBetween|spaceAround|spaceEvenly), crossAlign (min|center|max|baseline: first text baselines, horizontal layouts), contentAlign (wrapped lines: auto = packed where crossAlign says | spaceBetween), wrap (rows of a horizontal layout, columns of a vertical one), strokesIncluded (the frame's inside stroke takes up space), reverseZ (canvas stacking: true = first on top), columnGap / rowGap (aliases of gap / crossGap), gridColumns, gridRows, columnTracks / rowTracks ([120 | "1fr" | "auto" | {sizing, value}]), gridColumn / gridRow (0-based cell anchor, null = auto), gridColumnSpan, gridRowSpan, gridAlignH / gridAlignV (a grid child's alignment in its cell: min|center|max, auto/null = the frame's), sizingH / sizingV (fixed|hug|fill), absolute (ignore auto layout; follows constraints), minWidth, maxWidth, minHeight, maxHeight (null removes), constraints {horizontal, vertical}, grids, exports, characters, fontFamily, fontStyle, fontSize, lineHeight (auto|px|"150%"), letterSpacing (px|"2%"), textAlign (left|center|right|justified), textAlignVertical, textAutoResize (widthAndHeight|height|none|truncate), textDecoration, textDecorationStyle (solid|dotted|wavy), textDecorationThickness / textDecorationOffset (auto|px|"10%" of the font size; the offset runs from the baseline down to an underline's top edge), textDecorationSkipInk (underlines break around descenders), textDecorationColor (colour, or auto/null: the text's), textCase (original|upper|lower|title|smallCaps), paragraphSpacing, paragraphIndent, listStyle (none|bulleted|numbered; with start/end: the paragraphs those chars touch), indentation (list nesting level 0-8, same range rule), listSpacing (px between list items, in place of paragraphSpacing), hangingPunctuation, hangingList (markers outside the box), leadingTrim (vertical trim: none|capHeight), maxLines, features ({tag: bool}, e.g. {"liga": false, "tnum": true}), fontVariations / variationSettings ({axis: number}, e.g. {"wght": 550, "wdth": 85}; null = none), path (a vector's SVG path data: replaces its geometry, keeping the layer, its paints, styles and bindings; width/height in the same call scale it as node.create does; its own box goes at the layer's x/y, or with x/y given, at x + its left edge and y + its top as node.create places it), pointCount, innerRadius, arcStart, arcSweep, arcInner, booleanOperation (a boolean group's operation, or an operand's own; null: the group's), operandOperation (a layer in a boolean group: how it combines with the operands below it; null: the group's), constrainProportions, description, interactions, overflow, pluginData {k: v}
selection.createColorStyle* — Create selection color style {targets, name, description?} → {id}; makes a color style of the paint the targets share and applies it to them as selection.applyColorStyle does, keeping the variables bound to the paint; a name another style has, a target whose list holds other paints, or targets bound to different variables are refused
selection.bindColorVariable* — Apply selection color variable {targets, variable (id or name)}; binds the color variable to matching solid fill/stroke slots, replacing a color style there (text ranges with fills of their own take its value in the layer's modes)
selection.detachColor* — Detach selection color {targets}; unlinks the color style or variable of matching fill/stroke lists, keeping their values
file.open — Open [File] (Cmd+O) {path | data (base64) + name (tells the format; opens as a new unsaved document), variables? (REST: the local variables JSON as an object, JSON text or a path; default `<name>.variables.json` or `variables.json` next to the file), reload? (a file already open: read it again into its tab, which must have no unsaved changes)} (.figcraft, .json: FigCraft or REST API file JSON, .fig (best effort), .penpot, .sketch (Sketch 48 or newer, best effort), .svg, .png, .jpg …); REST, .fig, .penpot and .sketch imports return `warnings`; a file opened anew returns `summary` {name, pages, layers, images} (one that was already open returns its `index`, with `stale: true` when the file changed on disk since the tab read or saved it, or `reloaded: true` after `reload`)
file.import* — Import [File] (Shift+Cmd+I) {path | data (base64) + name, x?, y?, center? (SVG: centre it on x, y), variables? (REST: the local variables JSON as an object, JSON text or a path)}  SVG becomes an editable frame (shapes, text, gradients, masks, effects; with `warnings` for what it left out), images become image layers, .figcraft, .penpot, REST API file JSON, .fig and .sketch pages are appended with their variables and flows (REST, .fig, .penpot and .sketch: with `warnings`; those return `summary` {name, pages, layers, images} of the file read)
text.setVariations* — Variable font axes {variations: {axis: number | null (style default)}, replace? (clear others first), id?/ids?}; while editing: the selected range
text.missingFonts — Missing fonts [Text] {}  fonts the open document names that aren't installed (text layers, styled ranges, text styles, font family variables); the app shows them → {families: [{family, layers, source (the font store source font.download gets it from, or null)}]}
style.bind* — Bind variable in style {style, field, variable? (id or name; none: unbind)}  bind a variable to a field of the style's value: a paint style's `fills/<i>/color` (or `fill`: its first paint) and `fills/<i>/stops/<j>/color`, an effect style's `effects/<i>/<color|radius|spread|offsetX|offsetY|startRadius>` (glass: `lightAngle|lightIntensity|refraction|depth|dispersion|radius|splay`), a grid style's `layoutGrids/<i>/<size|count|gutter|offset>`, a text style's `fontSize|lineHeight|letterSpacing` (numbers, px) and `fontFamily|fontStyle` (strings). Every layer using the style shows the field resolved in its own modes; the style keeps it resolved in the default modes
variable.createCollection* — Create variable collection {name, modes? [names]}
variable.addMode* — Add mode {collection, name, from? (mode id or name to duplicate; default: the default mode)}
variable.create* — Create variable {collection, name, type: color|number|string|boolean, value (default mode) | values {modeName: value}, description?}  a value may also be {alias: variable} (same type); a colour value may also be {alpha: {variable, opacity 0..1}} (that variable's colour with its alpha replaced by the opacity) or {mix: {from, to, t}} (operands {variable: variable} or {literal: colour}; t is 0..1, 0 gives from and 1 to; blended per channel over the stored values, in the document's colour profile, including alpha; converting the profile keeps a mix's ends exact and moves its colours in between slightly), each alone in its object
variable.set* — Set variable value {variable, mode? (name or id; default first), value | {alias: variable} (same type, no loops) | {alpha} | {mix} (colour variables; shapes as in variable.create; no loops)}
variable.delete* — Delete variable {variable} (bound layers keep their values; variables aliasing it take its values; colour calculations reading it keep the colour they show)
variable.bind* — Bind variable {ids?, field (fill|stroke (first paint)|fills/<i>/color|strokes/<i>/color|fills/<i>/stops/<j>/color (gradient stops)|effects/<i>/<offsetX|offsetY|radius|startRadius|spread|color|lightAngle|lightIntensity|refraction|depth|dispersion|splay> (glass: `radius` is its frost; intensity, refraction, dispersion and splay in percent)|layoutGrids/<i>/<size|count|gutter|offset>|componentProperties/<name> (instances: boolean/text properties; variant properties take string variables naming a value)|width|height|opacity (percent)|cornerRadius|gap|paddingHorizontal|characters|visible|fontSize…; list indices bottom first), variable (null unbinds)}
variable.setMode* — Set variable mode {ids? (frames/page), collection, mode (id or name; null: Auto, inherited from the parent)}
variable.list — List variables {}
variable.update* — Edit variable {variable, name?, description?, scopes? ([scope ids]; null or ["ALL_SCOPES"] = every supported property, [] = hidden from pickers), hiddenFromPublishing? (left out when the file is published as a library), codeSyntax? {WEB?, iOS?, ANDROID?: name code uses ("" clears)}}
variable.duplicate* — Duplicate variable {variable} → {id}
variable.renameMode* — Rename mode {collection, mode, name}
variable.removeMode* — Delete mode {collection, mode} (a collection keeps at least one mode)
variable.moveMode* — Move mode {collection, mode, to (index; 0 = the default mode, layers on Auto follow it)}
variable.renameCollection* — Rename collection {collection, name}
variable.deleteCollection* — Delete collection {collection} (with its variables; bound layers keep their values; variables elsewhere aliasing them take their values and colour calculations reading them keep the colour they show)
variable.resetOverride* — Reset variable override {variable (a variable of an extended collection inherited from the collection it extends), mode? (id or name; every overridden mode when omitted)}  the value follows the inherited one again
variable.extendCollection* — Extend collection {collection (id or name of a collection of this file), name? (default "<name> (extended)")}  → {id}: a collection with its modes and variables that follows its edits (an extended collection can be extended again); override their values per mode with variable.set (variable.resetOverride goes back to the inherited value)
variable.export — Export variables {collections? [ids or names; default every collection of this file, not library copies], format? (json (default): the local variables JSON that variable.import reads, colour calculations as the colour they show in each mode with other collections in their default modes | css: custom properties, the default mode on :root and each other mode on [data-<collection>="<mode>"], colour calculations as the colour they show in that mode with other collections in their default modes; numbers in px unless layers or scopes use them as opacity or font weight | tailwind: a Tailwind CSS v4 stylesheet, the default mode as an @theme block named the way inspect.code's tailwind utilities read them: --color-*, --radius-*, --text-*, --spacing-*, --font-*, unique per file; each other mode as in css; colour calculations as the colour they show in that mode, other collections in their default modes) | dart: a Dart file for Flutter, a class of constants per collection and mode (Color, double, String, bool), aliases and colour calculations resolved), path? (write it there)}  → {text}, or {path} when written
variable.import* — Import variables {variables (the local variables JSON, as variable.export writes it: an object, JSON text or a path to a regular file of at most 256 MiB; `variableCollections` and `variables` under `meta` or at the top level)}  collections join this file's collection of the same name (values by mode name; new modes and variables are added, a variable of another type is skipped), others are added  → {collections (added), variables (added), updated, warnings (also when it holds no variables, or fewer than its collections list)}
library.publish* — Publish library {description?, include? [component/set ids, style ids, variable collection ids or names: exactly these], exclude? [same]}  publishes this file's components, component sets, styles and variable collections (by default all but names starting with . or _, or what the last publish offered; variables hidden from publishing stay out unless something published uses them) as a new library version; save the file so other files see it
library.list — List libraries {assets? (also list each library's components, styles, variable collections and variables, and what this file can publish)}  → enabled libraries (version, updates, errors) and this file's published library
library.publishToServer — Publish library to server {server? (an edit link of this file on a figcraft-server; omit while this file is in a live session on a server, or give the server's address with its key to keep the file there first), key?, description?, include?, exclude? (as library.publish)}  publishes the library as the next version of the one kept on the server under this file (per-asset versions as library.publish); files that enabled it with a link of the file see the update → {id, version, components, styles, collections, variables, file?, edit?, view? (links when the file was kept there now)}
library.swap* — Swap library {from (an enabled library: id, name or path), to (another enabled library)}  re-points every component instance, style and variable copied from `from` to the published one of the same name in `to` (instances keep their overrides) → {components, styles, variables, unmatched: [names still from `from`], removed (nothing of `from` is used any more: it was removed)}
library.updates — Library updates {}  → the components, styles, variable collections and variables with a newer published version, and variables new to a library collection this file extends (listed without an `id`: no copy yet)
library.acceptUpdates* — Accept library updates {ids? [library ids; all when omitted]}  pulls updated components, styles, variable collections and variables in (instances keep their overrides; bound layers follow)
library.importVariable* — Import library variable {library, variable (id or name of a published variable)}  → {variable (local, read-only linked copy to use with variable.bind, or as an alias in variable.set)}
library.bindVariable* — Bind library variable {library, variable (id or name of a published variable), field (as variable.bind), ids?}  copies the variable in (linked, read-only) and binds it
library.aliasVariable* — Alias library variable {library, alias (id or name of a published variable of the same type), variable (a local variable), mode? (default first)}  copies the library variable in (linked, read-only) and makes the local variable's value an alias of it
library.setVariableMode* — Set library variable mode {library, collection (id or name of a published collection), mode (id or name), ids? (frames; the page when omitted)}  copies the collection in (linked, read-only) and sets its mode on the frames
library.extendCollection* — Extend library collection {library, collection (id or name of a published collection), name? (default "<name> (extended)")}  → {id}: a collection of this file with the library collection's modes and variables (they follow its updates); override their values per mode with variable.set (variable.resetOverride goes back to the inherited value) and add variables of its own
proto.interaction.add* — Add interaction {id?, trigger? {type: onClick|onHover|onPress|onDrag|mouseEnter|mouseLeave|mouseDown|mouseUp|afterDelay {ms}|keyPress {key (a key or a combination: Shift+K, Ctrl+Alt+Delete; or a controller button: Gamepad A|B|X|Y|LB|RB|LT|RT|View|Menu|LS|RS|Up|Down|Left|Right|Home)}}, action {type: navigate {preserveScroll?}|back|scrollTo {offset? [x, y] (where the layer ends up from the top-left)}|openOverlay {position?, anchor? screen|triggerInside|triggerOutside (default screen; the trigger ones measure the position preset on the layer that opens the overlay: outside puts top presets above it and bottom presets below it, edges lined up), offset? [x, y] (position manual: the overlay's top-left from the top-left of the layer that opens it; without it, right below that layer), close_on_outside? (default true), background?}|swapOverlay|closeOverlay|openUrl {url, openInNewTab? (default true; false opens it in place of the prototype where the viewer's tab can go there: the web build)}|changeTo|setVariable {variable, value | expression (text, e.g. "count + 1")}|setVariableMode {collection, mode}|conditional {blocks [{condition? | expression? (text, e.g. "count >= 3"), actions}]}, dest?}, actions? [..], dest? (without action: a click-navigate to it), transition? {type: instant|dissolve|smartAnimate|moveIn|moveOut|push|slideIn|slideOut, direction?: left|right|top|bottom}, durationMs? | duration_ms?, easing? linear|easeIn|easeOut|easeInOut|easeInBack|easeOutBack|easeInOutBack|gentle|quick|bouncy|slow|{customBezier {x1, y1, x2, y2}}|{customSpring {mass, stiffness, damping}}, delayMs? | delay_ms? (mouse enter, leave, down and up: how long after the gesture the actions run, up to 600000)} — or {id, dest} for a click-navigate. Returns {index}
proto.action.add* — Add prototype action {id?, index (interaction), path? (where it goes: [n] appends to an interaction with n actions, [i, b, j] inside block b of the conditional i; default: after the last action), action {type: …, as proto.interaction.add; setVariable takes `expression` text, conditional blocks take `expression` or `condition`}} → {path}
proto.conditional.addBlock* — Add else if / else {id?, index, path (a conditional action), else? bool (add the else block; default: an else if before it), expression? (text, e.g. "count >= 3") | condition? (expression JSON); default condition: the first variable equal to its value} → {block}
proto.evaluate — Evaluate prototype expression {expression (text, e.g. "count + 1", "accent[Dark]", "mode(Theme) == 'Dark'") | expr (expression JSON), id? (the layer it runs on: variables resolve in its modes; default: the document's default modes)} → {value, type, text}  without changing anything
inspect.code — Code for layer {id?, language?: css|html|react|leptos|vue|tailwind|swiftui|compose|arkui|flutter (default css; html, react, leptos and vue are the whole layer tree; components take their properties as parameters, instances pass their values; a component connected to code (codeConnect.set) gives its import and snippet instead; tailwind is React with Tailwind CSS v4 utilities for pages: fluid auto layout boxes, instances inlined with their overrides, bound variables as theme utilities), mobile? (tailwind: a mobile frame with the same layer names; the code is mobile first with the desktop layer's classes behind lg:), unit?: px|rem (CSS, HTML, React, Leptos and Vue; default px), rootFontSize? (rem: pixels per rem, default 16)} → {code, language, connected}
inspect.properties — Inspect properties {id?, colorFormat?: hex|rgb|css|hsl|hsb (default hex)} → {sections: [{title, rows: [{label, value, color?, token?}]}]}  layout (positions from the frame around the layer), auto layout, typography, fills, strokes and effects, with style and variable names
